    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51651" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθᾰγ-νίζω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιῶ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>purify, hallow</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν τόπον θείῳ καὶ δᾳδί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Philops.</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτηρ πυρὶ καθήγνισται
			δέμας</span>, i.e. has been burnt on the funeral-pyre, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				40
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>offer as an expiatory sacrifice</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέλανον ἐπὶ πυρὶ καθαγνίσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ion</u>
					707
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).—On <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1081
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.190
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				558
			</span></i>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθαγίζω</span>
			.</div>
